---
import Document from '../../layouts/Document.astro';
import Snippet from '../../components/Snippet.astro';
import { localeParams, localePath } from '../../lib/i18n';

export const getStaticPaths = localeParams;
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const L = (p: string) => localePath(lang, p);
const endpoints = [
  ['/levels.json', 'The canonical vocabulary: definitions, decision procedure, edge cases and suggested mappings. Localised copies are available at /<lang>/levels.json.'],
  ['/spec.schema.json', 'JSON Schema for the vocabulary file itself.'],
  ['/levels.schema.json', 'JSON Schema for a declaration: level 0–5, optional surfaces, translation and review information.'],
  ['/ecosystem.json', 'A directory of related standards and projects; listing does not imply endorsement.'],
  ['/llms.txt', 'A short text index for tools that choose to read this convention. Google does not require it.'],
  ['/llms-full.txt', 'The full English vocabulary as plain text, including its limitations.'],
  ['/feed.xml', 'A release feed. Pin a release when reproducibility matters.'],
  ['/sitemap-index.xml', 'Canonical pages and the translations that are actually available.'],
];
const install = `git clone https://github.com/karauda/ai-usage-scale.git
cd ai-usage-scale/mcp
npm ci
node server.js`;
const mcpConfig = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "usagescale": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/ai-usage-scale/mcp/server.js"]
    }
  }
}`;
---
<Document sections={[
    { href: '#endpoints', label: 'Static endpoints' },
    { href: '#mcp', label: 'Local MCP server' },
    { href: '#declarations', label: 'Declare the work' }
  ]} navLabel="Integrations" lang={lang} path="/integrations" translated={false}
  title="Integrations — AI Usage Scale"
  description="Machine-readable vocabulary, validation schemas, declaration examples and a local MCP server."
  breadcrumb={[[ 'Integrations', '/integrations' ]]}>
  <header slot="header" class="prose">
    <p class="label">Developer reference</p>
    <h1>Integrations</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">Use the public definitions directly, or keep a versioned copy in your publishing tools.</p>
    <p>The vocabulary and marks are CC0. Website prose is CC BY 4.0; code is MIT.
      Requests to hosted endpoints reach the hosting provider. Inline SVG and downloaded copies work independently.</p>
  </header>
  <section id="endpoints" class="prose">
    <h2>Static endpoints</h2>
    <dl>{endpoints.map(([path, description]) => <div class="row">
      <dt><a href={path === '/levels.json' ? L(path) : path}><code>{path}</code></a></dt>
      <dd>{description}</dd>
    </div>)}</dl>
  </section>
  <section id="mcp" class="prose">
    <h2>Local MCP server</h2>
    <p>The repository includes a stdio server with four tools: <code>classify</code>, <code>get_level</code>,
      <code>list_levels</code> and <code>get_spec</code>, plus a <code>usagescale://levels.json</code> resource.
      Install its dependencies once; the server reads local data and makes no runtime network requests.</p>
    <p>As checked on 10 October 2026, <code>usagescale-mcp</code> is not published in the public npm registry.
      Install from the <a href="https://github.com/karauda/ai-usage-scale/tree/main/mcp">repository</a>:</p>
    <Snippet label="Install and run from source" code={install} />
    <Snippet label="MCP client configuration" code={mcpConfig} note="Replace the absolute path with your checkout location." />
    <p>The classifier returns a decision-tree suggestion. Verify the full definition, especially
      Level 3, which requires meaningful human review even though the current tree stops before asking about it.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="declarations" class="prose">
    <h2>Declare the work</h2>
    <p>Each <a href={L('/scale')}>level</a> provides a sentence, an SVG mark and metadata.
      The HTML metadata is a project convention. JSON-LD uses an explicitly namespaced extension;
      <code>aiUsageLevel</code> is not a registered Schema.org property.</p>
    <p>There is no dedicated Google Search feature for this scale. Do not use a declaration
      as a quality score, compliance certificate or evidence of permission to train a model.</p>
    <p>A publisher may choose <code>/.well-known/ai-disclosure.json</code> as a discovery location.
      That path is a project proposal, not a registered well-known URI. This website currently
      publishes no numeric self-declaration: the revised content awaits human editorial review.</p>
  </section>
</Document>
<style>
  .row { padding: 1rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-soft); }
  dt { font-weight: 600; }
  dd { margin: .4rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-mid); }
</style>
